creates formatted versions of the on‐line manual pages from their
source.  Manual pages whose formatted versions are missing or out
of  date  are regenerated.  If manual pages are regenerated, also
regenerates the database.  The optional argument is one word, and
contains the section numbers of all the sections to  be  checked.
For  example, if is ‘‘13f8’’, the manual pages in sections 1, 3f,
and 8 will be checked and regenerated.  If no  argument  is  pro‐
vided,  will  try to operate on all of the known manual sections.
The options are as follows: Ignore errors from nroff when  build‐
ing  manpages.  Do not create the database.  Display the commands
that would have been executed, but do not actually execute  them.
Perform work silently; do not echo commands as they are executed.
